# served-endurance.dl6 -- the served engine's endurance receipt program
# (plans/2026-07-29-runtime-bridge-header.md scope 5), driven by
# v6/tsv2/scripts/endurance.sh.
#
# The host writes ITS OWN TAG to a marks file BEFORE it sleeps, so the file
# counts SPAWNS STARTED, not answers delivered. That ordering is deliberate: a
# `kill -9` of the server does not kill the shell it already spawned, so a mark
# written after the sleep would still land and the count would say nothing about
# whether the restart refired anything.
#
# `$TSV2_MARKS` and `$TSV2_NAP` are ordinary environment references, inherited by
# the spawned shell like any other process environment. The template's declared
# input is `{tag}`; the compiler checks every declared input is referenced and
# that no output is, and leaves environment names alone.

rel seed(tag: text).

rel nap(tag: text) -> (value: text).

rel woke(tag: text, value: text).
woke(tag, value) <- seed(tag), nap(tag, value).
